WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.550
Translation memory stores earlier
source and target segments,

2
00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.756
and a tool searches it for exact,

3
00:00:06.756 --> 00:00:09.031
in-context, and fuzzy matches.

4
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:14.015
With AI, you still want approved
wording reused and past translations

5
00:00:14.015 --> 00:00:14.943
as context.

6
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:19.237
General Translation reuses earlier
translations and keeps your

7
00:00:19.237 --> 00:00:20.177
team's edits.

8
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:26.282
Run npx gt translate, and only
content whose source changed

9
00:00:26.282 --> 00:00:27.640
is translated again.

10
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.476
A matching translation from an
earlier file version is reused.

11
00:00:31.876 --> 00:00:34.755
Reviewers edit translations
in the Dashboard,

12
00:00:34.755 --> 00:00:39.944
and you can sync edits from downloaded
files with npx gt save-local.

13
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:43.064
Your team now ships
French with each release.
